      "type": "text",
      "options": {"content": "<h4>Latency boundaries</h4><p><b>Client task → all pre-Send</b> ends only when every child transport task has reached the provider <code>Send()</code> boundary. It includes client queueing, routing, splitting, transport enqueueing and executor queueing/preparation.</p><p><b>Transport task → pre-Send</b> is the same boundary for one child transport task. <b>Transport task → Send return</b> adds the provider Send call itself. <b>Send return → completion</b> is the completion-worker/CQE path. <b>End-to-end</b> is the whole client task from API entry to final aggregation.</p><p><b>Fake backend breakdown</b> is emitted only by the fake provider. Worker queue wait runs from provider <code>Send()</code> enqueue through fake-worker start. Process to CQE publish runs from fake-worker start through the release-store in <code>PublishCompletion</code>; it includes <code>fake_backend.latency_us</code> sleep and fake KV processing.</p>", "mode": "html"}
